course: dictionary
lesson: 8319
title: Robotic: machines and stiff voices
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Robotic is an adjective with two main meanings. The first is to do with robots, or done by a robot: a robotic arm. The second describes someone or something that moves or speaks stiffly, without feeling, like a robot: a robotic voice.
explain: Use the words around it to choose the right meaning. «In robotic surgery the surgeon sits at a console and controls the robot arms.» Here a machine does the job, so robotic means the first meaning. Check it by swapping in robot: robot surgery still makes sense.
explain: Now read «turned up, give a robotic effect on purpose.» This is about a sound, not a machine, and the effect is stiff and unnatural, so it means the second meaning. Ask yourself: is a machine doing the work, or does something sound or move stiffly, without feeling?
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Robotic» means to do with robots, or done by a robot.
fact: «Robotic» can also mean moving or speaking stiffly, without feeling, like a robot.
fact: Robotic arms work in factories, and robotic rovers move around on Mars by themselves.
fact: In the song «Believe» from 1998, Cher made a robotic Auto-Tune effect famous.
exercise: «In robotic surgery the surgeon controls the robot arms.» What does robotic mean here? | Stiff and without feeling | Very fast and dangerous | *To do with robots, done by a robot | Happy and friendly
exercise: Ella says her friend's reply sounded robotic. What does she mean? | *Stiff and without feeling, like a robot | Warm and full of laughter | Loud and cheerful | Sleepy and soft
exercise: Which of these is a robotic machine that moves by itself? | A pencil case | *A robotic vacuum cleaner | A wooden spoon | A cuddly teddy bear
test: Tom answers every question in a flat, stiff voice, with no feeling at all. What does robotic suggest about Tom? | Very tall and strong | Full of joy and energy | Hungry for lunch | *Bored, tired, or acting without feeling
test: «A robotic rover on Mars» is an example of what meaning? | Red and rocky | *To do with robots, moving by itself | Happy and friendly | Very slow and sleepy
exam: What is the best meaning of robotic in «robotic surgery»? | Quiet and gentle | *To do with robots, done by a robot | Stiff and without feeling | Dangerous and treacherous
